   },
   {
    "text": "Geoffrey Thün",
    "layer": "Name",
    "path": "Directors spreads/Spread rv-spread/Text column"
   },
   {
    "text": "Director of Design Research, RVTR. Professor of Architecture, Taubman College; Associate Vice President for Research, University of Michigan",
    "layer": "Role",
    "path": "Directors spreads/Spread rv-spread/Text column"
   },
   {
    "text": "Geoffrey Thün is a designer, researcher and educator, and a director of RVTR, which he co-founded in Toronto in 2007 with Kathy Velikov, Colin Ripley and Paul Raff; he leads the lab’s design research. He is Professor of Architecture at Taubman College of Architecture and Urban Planning and Associate Vice President for Research: Social Sciences, Humanities, and the Arts at the University of Michigan, where he is the research office’s liaison to those units. He is also co-director of the university’s Urban Collaboratory.",
    "layer": "",
    "path": "Directors spreads/Spread rv-spread/Text column"
   },
   {
    "text": "Taubman College profile",
    "link": "https://taubmancollege.umich.edu/faculty/directory/geoffrey-thun/",
